  "body": "Part of #658. Filed on the maintainer's word (question dialog, 2026-11-12); ours either way: it makes the UI usable with assistive technology and the structural tests able to find every control, and egui_kittest 0.37 fails tests on input widgets without one.\n\nToday about 58 input sites in `crates/ui` (`ComboBox`, `TextEdit`, `DragValue`, `Slider`) have no accessible name; only 6 call a labelling helper (figures from the estimate on #658, comment of 2026-11-12). A name is the visible label the row already shows (`labelled_by`) or, where there is none, a plain-English name.\n\nDone means: each of those widgets carries a name; a structural test walks the pages and fails on an unnamed input; the ui suites are green on egui 0.36.2 (no version bump here); no snapshot PNG touched. Can be done page family by page family, each PR with `Refs` until the guard test lands with the last.",
